    "abstract": "Illustrated parts figure for the trim air zone valve installation at the forward and aft distribution stations, showing the pre-modification and post-modification valve standards on separate sheets.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure identifies the trim air zone valve, its accumulator, the inlet filter and the mounting hardware at the forward and the aft distribution stations of the ceiling run.",
      "figure_note": "Sheet 1 shows the installation at the earlier standard with the plain valve body and no duct sensor boss; sheet 2 shows the same station at the standard 2 configuration with the switched assembly and the accumulator. The third sensing station shown on sheet 2 is fitted on ZEPHYR-24 aircraft only. Items marked as an alternate carry the effectivity that applies to their build standard and must not be mixed on one aircraft, because a zone would be left unsensed."
    },
